const math1: Question[] = [
  { image: IMG + 'm3-q1.png', text: 'In the triangle shown, PQ = QR. What is the value of x?', choices: c('156', '66', '48', '24'), answer: 'D' },
  { text: '4x + 1 = 33\n\nWhich equation has the same solution as the given equation?', choices: c('4x = 32', '4x = 5', '4x = 1', '4x = −32'), answer: 'A' },
  { text: 'For the linear function f, the graph of y = f(x) in the xy-plane has a slope of 7 and passes through the point (0, 5). Which equation defines f?', choices: c('f(x) = 5x', 'f(x) = 35x', 'f(x) = 7x + 5', 'f(x) = 12x + 5'), answer: 'C' },
  { text: '8x² − 40 = 32\n\nWhat is the positive solution to the given equation?', choices: c('3', '4', '9', '72'), answer: 'A' },
  { text: 'A total of 50 children attended a summer camp and were offered 4 types of sandwiches. The number of children who chose each type: Turkey — 15, Chicken — 23, Ham — 3, Vegetarian — 9 (jami 50).\n\nIf one of these children is selected at random, what is the probability of selecting a child who chose a vegetarian sandwich?', choices: c('9/100', '9/50', '1/4', '9/10'), answer: 'B' },
  { text: 'Amara grows cherry tomatoes in her backyard. This year, she harvested 750 cherry tomatoes and gave 10% of them to her neighbor. How many of the harvested cherry tomatoes did Amara give to her neighbor?', answer: '75' },
  { text: 'x + y = 125\nx + y + y = 155\n\nThe solution to the given system of equations is (x, y). What is the value of y?', answer: '30' },
  { text: 'In a chess tournament, each participant earns 1 point for each game the participant plays that ends in a draw and 3 points for each game the participant wins. A certain participant in this tournament has earned 41 points. Which equation represents this situation, where d represents the number of games this participant has played that ended in a draw and w represents the number of games this participant has won?', choices: c('d + 3w = 41', '3d + w = 41', 'd + w/3 = 41', 'd/3 + w = 41'), answer: 'A' },
  { text: 'The function g is defined by g(x) = √x + 300. What is the value of g(x) when x = 81?', choices: c('9', '300', '309', '381'), answer: 'C' },
  { text: 'A cable provider wanted to know how many of its 30,000 customers would be interested in a new service plan. The provider selected 300 customers at random and asked each customer whether the customer would be interested in the new plan. Of those surveyed, 8 said they would be interested. Which of the following is the best estimate of the total number of customers who would be interested in the new service plan?', choices: c('8', '80', '800', '8,000'), answer: 'C' },
  { text: 'Which expression is equivalent to 64t²s³ − 56t³s?', choices: c('4ts(16s² − 14ts)', '4ts(16t²s² − 14t)', '4t²s(16ts − 14s)', '4t²s(16s² − 14t)'), answer: 'D' },
  { text: 'x + 5 = 14\ny = 4x² + 4\n\nAt what point (x, y) do the graphs of the equations in the given system intersect?', choices: c('(9, 324)', '(9, 328)', '(14, 4)', '(14, 788)'), answer: 'B' },
  { text: '8x + 11y = 170\n\nThe equation gives the possible combinations of the number of 2009 premium grade Log Cabin Pennies, x, and the number of 1996 select grade Lincoln Pennies, y, in a collection that is worth a total of $170. If there are 6 1996 select grade Lincoln Pennies in the collection, how many 2009 premium grade Log Cabin Pennies are in the collection?', answer: '13' },
  { text: 'The population of the town of Smithville doubled every 75 years from 1659 to 1959. The population of this town was 240,000 in 1959. What was the population of this town in 1659?', answer: '15000' },
  { image: IMG + 'm3-q15.png', text: 'The scatterplot shows the relationship between x and y. A line of best fit is also shown.\n\nWhich of the following is closest to the slope of this line of best fit?', choices: c('0.60', '2.50', '7.80', '8.00'), answer: 'A' },
  { text: 'Which quadratic equation has exactly one distinct real solution?', choices: c('(x + 15)² = 0', '(x + 15)² = −45', '(x + 15)² = 45', '(x + 15)² = 135'), answer: 'A' },
  { text: 'The cost to rent a bus from Company X is $950 for the first 3 hours and an additional $50 per hour for each hour after the first 3 hours. If the total cost to rent the bus from Company X for t hours, where t > 3, is $1,150, which equation represents this situation?', choices: c('950(t − 3) + 50 = 1,150', '950(3t) + 50t = 1,150', '950 + 50(t − 3) = 1,150', '950 + 50(3t) = 1,150'), answer: 'C' },
  { image: IMG + 'm3-q18.png', text: 'x + y = 53\n11x + 18y = 730\n\nThe given equations represent the possible numbers of beach chairs, x, and umbrellas, y, rented at a park last month and the total spent, in dollars, to rent those beach chairs and umbrellas. Which of the following graphs represents this situation?', choices: c('Graph A', 'Graph B', 'Graph C', 'Graph D'), answer: 'B' },
  { image: IMG + 'm3-q19.png', text: 'In triangle QRS shown, QR < RS. Which expression represents the length of QS?', choices: c('18 cos Q', '18 sin Q', '18 / cos Q', '18 / sin Q'), answer: 'D' },
  { text: 'Circle A in the xy-plane has the equation (x + 5)² + (y − 5)² = 25. Circle B has the same center as circle A. The radius of circle B is two times the radius of circle A. The equation defining circle B in the xy-plane is (x + 5)² + (y − 5)² = k, where k is a constant. What is the value of k?', answer: '100' },
  { text: 'x² + 7x + 5 = 0\n\nOne solution to the given equation can be written as x = (−7 + √k) / 2, where k is a constant. What is the value of k?', answer: '29' },
  { text: 'A scientist measured the lengths of 240 gray seals from Muskeget Island and 120 gray seals from Sable Island. The scientist determined that the mean length of the 240 gray seals from Muskeget Island was 88 inches and the mean length of the 120 gray seals from Sable Island was 94 inches. What was the mean length of all 360 gray seals the scientist measured for this study?', choices: c('89', '90', '91', '92'), answer: 'B' },
  { image: IMG + 'm3-q23.png', text: 'The graph of y = f(x) + 4 is shown. Which equation defines function f?', choices: c('f(x) = −3ˣ + 1', 'f(x) = −3ˣ + 5', 'f(x) = −3ˣ + 8', 'f(x) = −3ˣ + 9'), answer: 'B' },
  { text: 'Two lines intersect at exactly one point, forming two acute angles and two obtuse angles. The measure of one of these angles is (9x − 140)°. Which of the following could NOT be the sum of the measures of any two of these angles?', choices: c('(−18x + 280)°', '(−18x + 640)°', '(18x − 280)°', '180°'), answer: 'A' },
  { text: '2x + 9y = 7\n\nThe given equation is one equation in a system of two linear equations. If the system of equations has at least one solution, which of the following equations could be the other equation in the system?\n\nI. 3x + 13.5y = 10.5\nII. 3x − 13.5y = 10.5', choices: c('I only', 'II only', 'I and II', 'Neither I nor II'), answer: 'C' },
  { text: 'A right rectangular prism has a base area of 24t square centimeters (cm²). The length of the base of the rectangular prism is 8/3 cm, and the height of the rectangular prism is 15 cm. Which expression represents the surface area, in cm², of the right rectangular prism?', choices: c('48t + 160', '318t + 80', '1,968t + 80', '360t'), answer: 'B' },
  { text: 'For a particular car, the linear function f gives the predicted power, in brake horsepower (bhp), for engine speeds between 1,000 revolutions per minute (rpm) and 6,000 rpm. According to this function, the car’s predicted power is 433 bhp at an engine speed of 3,331 rpm and 600 bhp at an engine speed of 4,500 rpm. The equation f(x) = (1/7)(x − a) + 433 defines f, where x is the engine speed, in rpm, and a is a constant. What is the value of a?', answer: '3331' },
];

